        /// <summary>
        /// 
        /// </summary>
        /// <remarks>
        /// One hop out from a subject, each neighbour carrying its own fact count so a relation chip is navigable rather than decorative - without it the caller needs one request per chip. Paginated by cursor over the edge&#39;s own &#x60;(created_at, id)&#x60;: a neighbour&#39;s fact count changes under ingest, so it cannot carry a stable cursor. &#x60;limit&#x60; is capped lower than the general list limit because each row costs three correlated counts. &#x60;count&#x3D;true&#x60; returns the subject&#39;s visible edge total, and is refused alongside &#x60;minFacts&#x60; because that filter runs after each page is hydrated - honouring it in a total would cost the per-neighbour counts this walk exists to avoid.
        /// </remarks>
